{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md; sed -n '1045,1165p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go; sed -n '1470,1665p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go; rg -n 'func (discoverValidationModules|moduleValidationChecks)|type validationModule|func .*Validation.*odule|func IsAdministrativePath|func writeValidation|func .*ValidationResult' pose-mcp/internal\"","aggregated_output":"# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n\t}\n\tstartReflog := movementWitness(root, pinnedHead)\n\t// The working copy must match the pinned head before the plan inputs are\n\t// read, by the same full predicate checked at the end: status, hidden\n\t// index entries and submodule checkouts (review round 14, N40 and N41).\n\tstartedClean := pinnedHead != \"\" && validationMaterialClean(root, pinnedHead)\n\tmatrixPath := filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"indexes\", \"validation-matrix.json\")\n\traw, err := os.ReadFile(matrixPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: validation matrix not found at %s\\n\", \"Erro: matriz de validação não encontrada em %s\\n\"), matrixPath)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tmatrix, err := parseValidationMatrix(raw)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: invalid validation matrix: %v\\n\", \"Erro: matriz de validação inválida: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif err := validateStructuredMatrixPaths(matrix); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: invalid validation matrix path: %v\\n\", \"Erro: path inválido na matriz de validação: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif err := validateDeliveryMatrixContract(matrix); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: invalid delivery validation contract: %v\\n\", \"Erro: contrato de validação de delivery inválido: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif matrixHasLegacyChecks(matrix) {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: legacy shell 'command' checks are unsupported; migrate each check to program + args + env.\", \"Erro: checks shell legados em 'command' não são suportados; migre cada check para program + args + env.\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif mode == \"\" {\n\t\tmode = matrix.Defaults.Mode\n\t\tif mode == \"\" {\n\t\t\tmode = \"strict\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tmodules, err := discoverValidationModules(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: discovering modules: %v\\n\", \"Erro: descobrir módulos: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tif workspaceFilter != \"\" {\n\t\tresolved, ok := resolveWorkspaceModulePath(root, modules, workspaceFilter)\n\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: no module's manifest name matches --workspace %q.\\n\", \"Erro: nenhum module tem name de manifesto igual a --workspace %q.\\n\"), workspaceFilter)\n\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t}\n\t\tmoduleFilter = resolved\n\t}\n\tknownModules := map[string]bool{}\n\tfor _, module := range modules {\n\t\tknownModules[module.Rel] = true\n\t}\n\tfor rel, override := range matrix.ModuleOverrides {\n\t\tclean := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(rel))\n\t\tif clean == \"..\" || strings.HasPrefix(clean, \"../\") || filepath.IsAbs(rel) {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: moduleOverrides contains a path outside the project: %s\\n\", \"Erro: moduleOverrides contém path fora do projeto: %s\\n\"), rel)\n\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t}\n\t\tif knownModules[clean] {\n\t\t\tif override.Stack != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tfor idx := range modules {\n\t\t\t\t\tif modules[idx].Rel == clean {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tmodules[idx].Stack = override.Stack\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tabs := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(clean))\n\t\tif info, err := os.Stat(abs); err == nil && info.IsDir() {\n\t\t\tstack := override.Stack\n\t\t\tif stack == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tstack = \"contract\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tmodules = append(modules, validationModule{Rel: clean, Abs: abs, Stack: stack})\n\t\t\tknownModules[clean] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(modules, func(i, j int) bool { return modules[i].Rel < modules[j].Rel })\n\tvar scope *scopeSelection\n\tif changedTo != \"\" && changedFrom == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: --changed-to requires --changed-from.\", \"Erro: --changed-to exige --changed-from.\"))\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}\n\tif changedFrom != \"\" {\n\t\tsel, err := computeChangedScope(root, changedFrom, changedTo, modules)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: changed-scope selection: %v\\n\", \"Erro: seleção por escopo alterado: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\t\treturn 2\n\t\t}\n\t\tscope = &sel\n\t\tif explain {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"[changed-scope] %s: %d changed file(s), %d/%d module(s) selected\\n\", sel.rangeLabel(), len(sel.Changed), len(sel.Selected), len(modules))\n\t\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\t\t\tif reason, ok := sel.Selected[m.Rel]; ok {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"  + %s: %s\\n\", m.Rel, reason)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"  - %s: not affected by %s\\n\", m.Rel, sel.rangeLabel())\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\trun := validationRunResult{\n\t\tSchemaVersion: validationResultSchema,\n\t\tGeneratedAt:   time.Now().UTC().Format(time.RFC3339),\n\t\tMode:          mode,\n\t\tStackFilter:   stackFilter,\n\t\tModuleFilter:  moduleFilter,\n\t\tChecks:        []checkResult{},\n\t}\n\tmatrixDigest := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\trun.MatrixSHA256 = \"sha256:\" + hex.EncodeToString(matrixDigest[:])\n\trun.EngineVersion = validationEngineIdentity()\n\t// The head is pinned before anything is planned: selection, carried\n\t// results and the end-of-run comparison all name this one commit (review\n\t// round 5, N14).\n\trun.GitHead = pinnedHead\n\tvar carryState carryPlan\n\tif carry {\n\t\tcarryState = planCarry(root, canonicalResultsPath, mode, run.MatrixSHA256, run.GitHead, matrix, modules)\n\t\trun.Carry = carryState.record\n\tfor _, line := range validationTimingNotes(run) {\n\t\tsteps.Note(line)\n\t}\n\tsteps.Summary()\n\tif executed == 0 && run.Counts.Carried == 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(stdout, \"No modules/checks matched the matrix and filters.\")\n\t}\n\tresult := \"pass\"\n\tif cancelled {\n\t\tfailures++\n\t\tresult = \"fail\"\n\t\tr.Verdict(cliout.Verdict{State: cliout.StateFail, Text: cliText(locale, \"validation cancelled\", \"validação cancelada\")})\n\t} else if failures > 0 {\n\t\tresult = \"fail\"\n\t\tr.Verdict(cliout.Verdict{State: cliout.StateFail, Text: cliText(locale, \"required check failed\", \"check obrigatório falhou\")})\n\t} else {\n\t\tif optionalFailures > 0 {\n\t\t\tresult = \"partial\"\n\t\t\tr.Finding(cliout.Finding{State: cliout.StateWarning, Code: \"optional-check\",\n\t\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"%d optional check(s) failed\", \"%d check(s) opcional(is) falharam\"), optionalFailures)})\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.Verdict(cliout.Verdict{State: cliout.StatePass})\n\t}\n\trun.Outcome = result\n\tusageFindings := make([]usageFinding, 0, run.Counts.Failed+run.Counts.OptionalFailed+run.Counts.Errored)\n\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n\t\tif check.Outcome != \"fail\" && check.Outcome != \"error\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tseverity := check.Severity\n\t\tif check.Outcome == \"error\" {\n\t\t\tseverity = \"error\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tusageFindings = append(usageFindings, usageFinding{ID: check.ID, Severity: severity})\n\t}\n\tnoteUsageFindings(stdout, result, usageFindings, true)\n\tfor name, writer := range map[string]struct {\n\t\tpath  string\n\t\twrite func(string, validationRunResult) error\n\t}{\n\t\t\"json\":  {jsonOut, writeValidationJSON},\n\t\t\"junit\": {junitOut, writeValidationJUnit},\n\t\t\"sarif\": {sarifOut, writeValidationSARIF},\n\t} {\n\t\tif writer.path == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(writer.path))\n\t\tif name == \"json\" && canonicalResultsPath != \"\" && normalizeValidationOutputPath(writer.path) == canonicalResultsPath {\n\t\t\terr := publishCanonicalValidationJSONIn(store, writer.path, canonicalResultsPath, run)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tif errors.Is(err, posemodel.ErrPublishUnsynced) {\n\t\t\t\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\t\t\t\tout.ContractLine(fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", name, target))\n\t\t\t\t\tout.Finding(cliout.Finding{State: cliout.StateWarning, Code: \"validation-result-durability\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(\"%s result was published but durability is unconfirmed: %v\", name, err)})\n\t\t\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"writing %s result: %v\", \"escrevendo resultado %s: %v\"), name, err))\n\t\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).ContractLine(fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", name, target))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(target), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: creating %s result directory: %v\\n\", \"Erro: criando diretório do resultado %s: %v\\n\"), name, err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := writer.write(target, run); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: writing %s result: %v\\n\", \"Erro: escrevendo resultado %s: %v\\n\"), name, err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"%s: %s\\n\", name, target)\n\t}\n\tif planOut != \"\" {\n\t\tdigest := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\t\thead := \"\"\n\t\tif out, err := posemodel.RawHistoryGit(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").Output(); err == nil {\n\t\t\thead = strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n\t\t}\n\t\tplan := executionPlan{\n\t\t\tSchemaVersion: validationResultSchema,\n\t\t\tGeneratedAt:   run.GeneratedAt,\n\t\t\tProjectID:     posemodel.DefaultProjectID(root),\n\t\t\tSpec:          reportTask,\n\t\t\tGitHead:       head,\n\t\t\tMatrixSHA256:  hex.EncodeToString(digest[:]),\n\t\t\tChecks:        isolationChecks,\n\t\t\tApproval:      planApproval{Required: true},\n\t\t}\n\t\tif plan.Checks == nil {\n\t\t\tplan.Checks = []checkResult{}\n\t\t}\n\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(planOut))\n\t\tif err := writeExecutionPlan(target, plan); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: writing execution plan: %v\\n\", \"Erro: escrevendo plano de execução: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"plan: %s (%d isolated check(s); approval required before Harness execution)\\n\", target, len(plan.Checks))\n\t}\n\tif autoReport {\n\t\tif reportTask == \"\" {\n\t\t\treportTask = \"validate-native\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treportArgs := []string{\"--task\", reportTask, \"--context\", \"auto-validate\", \"--validation-profile\", mode}\n\t\t// The outcome travels inside the summary, so it stays derived rather\n\t\t// than being recorded as a manual assertion.\n\t\t_ = runReportWith(root, reportArgs, nil, validationSummaryOf(run), io.Discard, stderr)\n\t}\n\tif failures > 0 {\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\n// validationSummaryOf projects a finished run for `pose report`: the commands\n// it executed and one line per check, with the outcome the run reached. It is\n// the structured replacement for parsing the printed output (spec\n// pose-cli-output-rendering-system R5).\n// moduleValidationChecks resolves the stack and checks one module runs after\n// overrides, and whether the stack/module filters select it at all. The counting\n// pass and the executing pass share it so a filter can never mean two things\n// (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R6).\nfunc moduleValidationChecks(module validationModule, matrix validationMatrix, stackFilter, moduleFilter string) (string, []validationCheck, bool) {\n\toverride := matrix.ModuleOverrides[module.Rel]\n\tstack := module.Stack\n\tif override.Stack != \"\" {\n\t\tstack = override.Stack\n\t}\n\tif stackFilter != \"\" && stack != stackFilter || moduleFilter != \"\" && module.Rel != moduleFilter {\n\t\treturn stack, nil, false\n\t}\n\tchecks := append([]validationCheck(nil), matrix.Stacks[stack].Checks...)\n\tif override.ReplaceDefaultChecks {\n\t\tchecks = nil\n\t}\n\treturn stack, append(checks, override.Checks...), true\n}\n\n// tailLines keeps the last n lines of a check's captured output: enough to see\n// why it failed, with the full output one path away.\nfunc tailLines(text string, n int) string {\n\tlines := strings.Split(strings.TrimRight(text, \"\\n\"), \"\\n\")\n\tif len(lines) <= n {\n\t\treturn strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Join(lines[len(lines)-n:], \"\\n\")\n}\n\nfunc validationSummaryOf(run validationRunResult) *validationSummary {\n\tsummary := &validationSummary{Outcome: run.Outcome}\n\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n\t\tcommand := strings.TrimSpace(check.Program + \" \" + strings.Join(check.Args, \" \"))\n\t\tif check.Outcome != \"skipped\" && command != \"\" {\n\t\t\tsummary.Commands = append(summary.Commands, command)\n\t\t}\n\t\tline := \"- [\" + check.Outcome + \"] \" + check.ID\n\t\tswitch {\n\t\tcase check.SkipReason != \"\":\n\t\t\tline += \" (\" + check.SkipReason + \")\"\n\t\tcase check.DurationSeconds > 0:\n\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" (%.1fs)\", check.DurationSeconds)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif check.ExitCode != nil {\n\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" exit=%d\", *check.ExitCode)\n\t\t}\n\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, line)\n\t}\n\t// The report records the run's verdict too, built from the outcome rather\n\t// than copied from the printed line, so the recorded evidence keeps its\n\t// shape while the terminal is free to change.\n\tif run.Counts.OptionalFailed > 0 {\n\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, fmt.Sprintf(\"Warning: %d optional check(s) failed.\", run.Counts.OptionalFailed))\n\t}\n\tswitch run.Outcome {\n\tcase \"fail\":\n\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, \"Result: FAILURE (required check failed)\")\n\tdefault:\n\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, \"Result: SUCCESS\")\n\t}\n\treturn summary\n}\n\nfunc sanitizeGoCheckArgs(ctx context.Context, dir, program string, args []string) []string {\n\tif program != \"go\" || len(args) == 0 {\n\t\treturn args\n\t}\n\n\thasWildcard := false\n\tfor _, a := range args {\n\t\tif a == \"./...\" || strings.HasSuffix(a, \"/...\") {\n\t\t\thasWildcard = true\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif !hasWildcard {\npackage cli\n\n// Explainable changed-scope validation (spec pose-changed-scope-validation):\n// select the minimum safe set of modules from explicit Git revisions,\n// declared dependency edges and policy. Selection is deterministic for the\n// same base/head/config; every decision carries a reason and every\n// unselected check is recorded as skipped with a machine-readable reason.\n// Uncertainty always widens toward safe execution.\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// safeGitRevRE rejects revisions that could be parsed as options or escape\n// expected forms (confinement: never pass untrusted flags to git).\nvar safeGitRevRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/~^-]*$`)\n\ntype scopeModuleMeta struct {\n\tCriticality string   `json:\"criticality\"`\n\tDependsOn   []string `json:\"dependsOn\"`\n\t// SelfContained declares that the module's checks read only its own\n\t// directory and its declared dependencies, so a change outside every\n\t// module does not select it (spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks R6).\n\tSelfContained bool `json:\"selfContained\"`\n}\n\ntype scopeMetadata struct {\n\tModules map[string]scopeModuleMeta `json:\"modules\"`\n}\n\n// loadScopeMetadata reads the module metadata. An absent file is empty\n// metadata; a file that does not decode is an error, never a partial\n// reading that could keep an exemption and drop a dependency (review round\n// 3, N6).\nfunc loadScopeMetadata(root string) (scopeMetadata, error) {\n\tvar meta scopeMetadata\n\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"indexes\", \"module-metadata.json\"))\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn meta, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn meta, fmt.Errorf(\"module metadata is unreadable: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &meta); err != nil {\n\t\treturn scopeMetadata{}, fmt.Errorf(\"module metadata does not decode: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn meta, nil\n}\n\n// scopeSelection maps selected module → deterministic selection reason.\ntype scopeSelection struct {\n\tBase, Head string\n\tChanged    []string\n\tSelected   map[string]string\n}\n\nfunc (s scopeSelection) rangeLabel() string {\n\tif s.Head == \"\" {\n\t\treturn s.Base + \"..worktree\"\n\t}\n\treturn s.Base + \"..\" + s.Head\n}\n\n// computeChangedScope resolves the selection. Modules are selected when they\n// contain changed files, depend (transitively) on a changed module, or policy\n// widens them (criticality high). A change outside every module selects\n// every module that does not declare itself self-contained — uncertainty\n// prefers safe execution. Excluded paths (the run's own canonical result) are\n// not changes.\nfunc computeChangedScope(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule, exclude ...string) (scopeSelection, error) {\n\tmeta, err := loadScopeMetadata(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn scopeSelection{Base: base, Head: head, Selected: map[string]string{}}, err\n\t}\n\treturn computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head, modules, meta, exclude...)\n}\n\n// computeChangedScopeWith selects with the given metadata snapshot, so a\n// caller that verified one snapshot selects with exactly it (review round 17,\n// N50).\nfunc computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule, meta scopeMetadata, exclude ...string) (scopeSelection, error) {\n\tsel := scopeSelection{Base: base, Head: head, Selected: map[string]string{}}\n\tfor _, rev := range []string{base, head} {\n\t\tif rev != \"\" && !safeGitRevRE.MatchString(rev) {\n\t\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"unsafe git revision: %q\", rev)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// NUL-delimited and without rename pairing: a quoted or multi-line name\n\t// keeps its owner, and a rename names both its source and its destination\n\t// (review round 2, N1 and N3).\n\t// Configuration never hides a changed gitlink (review round 8, N23).\n\tgitArgs := []string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"diff.ignoreSubmodules=none\", \"diff\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"--no-renames\", base}\n\tif head != \"\" {\n\t\tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, head)\n\t}\n\tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, \"--\")\n\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(gitArgs...).Output()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?)\", sel.rangeLabel())\n\t}\n\tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n\t\tif name != \"\" {\n\t\t\tsel.Changed = append(sel.Changed, filepath.ToSlash(name))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif head == \"\" {\n\t\t// Worktree comparisons must also see untracked files — invisible new\n\t\t// code must never silently narrow validation (safe execution wins).\n\t\tif untracked, err := posemodel.RawHistoryGit(root, \"ls-files\", \"-z\", \"--others\", \"--exclude-standard\").Output(); err == nil {\n\t\t\tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(untracked), \"\\x00\") {\n\t\t\t\tif name != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tsel.Changed = append(sel.Changed, filepath.ToSlash(name))\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(exclude) > 0 {\n\t\texcluded := map[string]bool{}\n\t\tfor _, path := range exclude {\n\t\t\texcluded[filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(path))] = true\n\t\t}\n\t\tkept := sel.Changed[:0]\n\t\tfor _, file := range sel.Changed {\n\t\t\tif !excluded[file] {\n\t\t\t\tkept = append(kept, file)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tsel.Changed = kept\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(sel.Changed)\n\n\tmoduleOf := func(file string) string {\n\t\tmatch := \"\"\n\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\t\tif file == m.Rel || strings.HasPrefix(file, m.Rel+\"/\") {\n\t\t\t\tif len(m.Rel) > len(match) {\n\t\t\t\t\tmatch = m.Rel\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn match\n\t}\n\t// Every changed file selects, independently of one another (review rounds\n\t// 2–4, N2, N5, N7, N8):\n\t//   - its most specific owning module;\n\t//   - every module under it (a gitlink or a replaced directory changes what\n\t//     lies beneath);\n\t//   - every module whose declared dependsOn contains it, lies under it, or\n\t//     is the project root \".\", whether or not the dependency is discovered;\n\t//   - when no module owns it: the root module and every module that does\n\t//     not declare itself self-contained (safe execution wins).\n\tselectModule := func(rel, reason string) {\n\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[rel]; !ok {\n\t\t\tsel.Selected[rel] = reason\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tfor _, file := range sel.Changed {\n\t\towner := moduleOf(file)\n\t\tif owner != \"\" {\n\t\t\tselectModule(owner, \"contains changed file: \"+file)\n\t\t\t// An enclosing module's checks may read inside the modules nested\n\t\t\t// in its directory, and the root module encloses them all (review\n\t\t\t// round 9, N25).\n\t\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\t\t\tif m.Rel != owner && (m.Rel == \".\" || strings.HasPrefix(owner, m.Rel+\"/\")) {\n\t\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"changed file in nested module \"+owner+\": \"+file)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\t\tif m.Rel != \".\" && strings.HasPrefix(m.Rel, file+\"/\") {\n\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"changed path above the module: \"+file)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t// Every eligible dependency counts, whatever its order (review\n\t\t\t// round 5, N11).\n\t\t\t// A dependency that is the file's own owner reaches its dependents\n\t\t\t// through the transitive widening; any other one, discovered or not,\n\t\t\t// selects here (review round 6, N15).\n\t\t\tfor _, dep := range declaredDependencyHits(file, meta.Modules[m.Rel].DependsOn) {\n\t\t\t\tif dep != owner {\n\t\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"declared dependency \"+dep+\" changed: \"+file)\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif owner == \"\" && (m.Rel == \".\" || !meta.Modules[m.Rel].SelfContained) {\n\t\t\t\tselectModule(m.Rel, \"root-level change outside any module: \"+file)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// Policy widening: high-criticality modules always run.\n\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\tif meta.Modules[m.Rel].Criticality == \"high\" {\n\t\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[m.Rel]; !ok {\n\t\t\t\tsel.Selected[m.Rel] = \"policy: criticality high always runs\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// Transitive dependents of selected modules (declared edges only).\n\tfor changed := true; changed; {\n\t\tchanged = false\n\t\tfor _, m := range modules {\n\t\t\tif _, ok := sel.Selected[m.Rel]; ok {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfor _, dep := range meta.Modules[m.Rel].DependsOn {\n\t\t\t\tif reason, ok := sel.Selected[filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(dep))]; ok {\n\t\t\t\t\tsel.Selected[m.Rel] = \"depends on selected module \" + dep + \" (\" + firstScopeReason(reason) + \")\"\n\t\t\t\t\tchanged = true\n\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn sel, nil\n}\n\n// firstScopeReason keeps chained dependency reasons short and readable.\nfunc firstScopeReason(reason string) string {\n\tif i := strings.Index(reason, \" (\"); i > 0 {\n\t\treturn reason[:i]\n\t}\n\treturn reason\n}\n\n// declaredDependencyHits returns every declared dependency file changes: one\n// it lies in, one it lies above, or the project root \".\", which every file\n// changes.\nfunc declaredDependencyHits(file string, deps []string) []string {\n\tvar hits []string\n\tfor _, dep := range deps {\n\t\tdep = filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(dep))\n\t\tif dep == \".\" || file == dep || strings.HasPrefix(file, dep+\"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(dep, file+\"/\") {\n\t\t\thits = append(hits, dep)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn hits\n}\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_root_and_nodemodules_test.go:78:func TestDiscoverValidationModules_IgnoresQwenWorktrees(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_root_and_nodemodules_test.go:109:func TestDiscoverValidationModules_IgnoresFixtureDirectories(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_root_and_nodemodules_test.go:141:func TestDiscoverValidationModules_RespectsGitignore(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_root_and_nodemodules_test.go:176:func TestDiscoverValidationModules_ClassifiesAndroidSeparatelyFromJava(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/discovery_submodule_test.go:75:func TestDiscoverValidationModules_RespectsGitignoreInsideSubmodule(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:66:func loadDeliveryValidationResultsIn(files posemodel.Files, root, relative string) ([]posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:93:func withSmokeResults(root string, results []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult) []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:103:func withSmokeResultsIn(files posemodel.Files, root string, results []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult) []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:111:func appendVerifiedSmokeResults(results []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult, smoke []posemodel.SmokeResult) []posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:122:func loadDeliveryValidationResults(root, relative string) ([]posemodel.DeliveryValidationResult, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:655:type validationModule struct {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:667:func discoverValidationModulesIn(files posemodel.Files, root string) ([]validationModule, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:734:func discoverValidationModules(root string) ([]validationModule, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1593:func moduleValidationChecks(module validationModule, matrix validationMatrix, stackFilter, moduleFilter string) (string, []validationCheck, bool) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results_test.go:240:func configureCanonicalValidationResults(t *testing.T, root, relative string) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go:200:func writeValidationJSON(path string, run validationRunResult) error {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go:301:func writeValidationJUnit(path string, run validationRunResult) error {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go:348:func writeValidationSARIF(path string, run validationRunResult) error {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/stack_manifest_test.go:80:func TestDiscoverValidationModulesDetectsCloudflareWorkers(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_facts.go:219:func factResultKey(r DeliveryValidationResult) string {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/index_inputs_test.go:53:func TestValidationResultsBindingTracksOutcome(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_facts_review_regression_test.go:18:func factsWithResultsFile(t *testing.T, indexed []DeliveryValidationResult) (Store, func(edit func(run map[string]any))) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/evidence_gate_test.go:69:func dropValidationResults(t *testing.T, root string) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/material_binding.go:36:func IsAdministrativePath(p string) bool {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1687:func holdsValidationResult(evidence []ReviewBundleEvidence) bool {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:16:func ParseDeliveryValidationRun(raw []byte, relative string) ([]DeliveryValidationResult, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_surface.go:100:func resultCoversTarget(result DeliveryValidationResult, target DeliveryTarget) bool {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_surface.go:387:func BuildDeliverySurface(graph DeliveryIntegrityGraph, specs []Spec, targets []DeliveryTarget, results []DeliveryValidationResult, roadmaps []Roadmap, profiles map[string]DeliveryProfile, policy DeliveryPolicy) DeliveryIntegrityGraph {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_surface.go:624:func deliveryEvidenceCurrent(result DeliveryValidationResult, spec, status string, graph DeliveryIntegrityGraph, sets []ChangeSet) bool {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_facts_binding_test.go:15:func factsFixture(t *testing.T, components string, results []DeliveryValidationResult, publish bool) Store {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/spec_facts_binding_test.go:21:func factsFixtureWith(t *testing.T, components string, results []DeliveryValidationResult, publish bool, changeSets []ChangeSet) Store {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go:618:func (s Store) smokeResultsOf(doc smokeResultDocument, run ReviewRun, bundle ReviewBundle, rel string) []DeliveryValidationResult {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go:630:func smokeResultsInputOf(doc smokeResultDocument, run ReviewRun, bundle ReviewBundle, rel string) []DeliveryValidationResult {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delegated_verdicts.go:634:func smokeResultsWithProvenance(doc smokeResultDocument, run ReviewRun, bundle ReviewBundle, rel string, scoped map[string]string) []DeliveryValidationResult {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^func Test'\"' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_engine_identity_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run_test.go; git diff dec2e64..HEAD -- POSE.md locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go; rg -n -i 'carry|unchanged-checks' .pose/knowledge pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"127:func TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule(t *testing.T) {\n156:func TestCarryKeepsTheOriginalHeadAcrossChainedCarries(t *testing.T) {\n173:func TestCarryKeepsACarriedFailureAFailure(t *testing.T) {\n189:func TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun(t *testing.T) {\n242:func TestCarryRootChangeRunsEverythingUnlessSelfContained(t *testing.T) {\n265:func TestChangedScopeHonoursSelfContainedModules(t *testing.T) {\n274:func TestCarryRecordFileIsNotAChange(t *testing.T) {\n283:func TestCarrySelectsAModuleWithoutAPriorResult(t *testing.T) {\n309:func TestCarryRefusesAFilteredBase(t *testing.T) {\n321:func TestCarryRefusesIncompatibleFlags(t *testing.T) {\n334:func TestCarryIgnoresDerivedAdministrativeRecords(t *testing.T) {\n355:func TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy(t *testing.T) {\n378:func TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename(t *testing.T) {\n395:func TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName(t *testing.T) {\n411:func TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles(t *testing.T) {\n429:func TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n445:func TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata(t *testing.T) {\n461:func TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n477:func TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n492:func TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles(t *testing.T) {\n507:func TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink(t *testing.T) {\n526:func TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n539:func TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency(t *testing.T) {\n554:func TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial(t *testing.T) {\n581:func TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory(t *testing.T) {\n601:func TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead(t *testing.T) {\n628:func TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents(t *testing.T) {\n652:func TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink(t *testing.T) {\n669:func TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule(t *testing.T) {\n686:func TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths(t *testing.T) {\n707:func TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem(t *testing.T) {\n729:func TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs(t *testing.T) {\n746:func TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath(t *testing.T) {\n763:func TestChangedScopeIgnoresSubmoduleHidingConfiguration(t *testing.T) {\n772:func TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n785:func TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule(t *testing.T) {\n819:func TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n844:func TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule(t *testing.T) {\n857:func TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule(t *testing.T) {\n888:func TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor(t *testing.T) {\n909:func TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule(t *testing.T) {\n922:func TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries(t *testing.T) {\n955:func TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository(t *testing.T) {\n970:func TestCarryRefusesUncleanDependencies(t *testing.T) {\n983:func TestCarryRefusesNonASCIIPaths(t *testing.T) {\n996:func TestCarryRefusesHiddenIndexEntries(t *testing.T) {\n1018:func TestCarryRefusesDependenciesThroughAnIgnoredSymlink(t *testing.T) {\n1036:func TestValidateHeadMovingAndReturningIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1050:func TestCarryCaseProbeUsesOnlyASCIILetters(t *testing.T) {\n1078:func TestValidateModeChangeHiddenByConfigurationIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1094:func TestValidateUninitializedSubmoduleIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1118:func TestValidateConditionClearedDuringTheRunIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1135:func TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1166:func TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel(t *testing.T) {\n1184:func TestCarryRefusesWorkingMetadataThatDiffersFromHead(t *testing.T) {\n1197:func TestCancellationMakesBindingsUnavailable(t *testing.T) {\n1206:func TestValidateNestedSubmodulesAreNotClean(t *testing.T) {\n1241:func TestCarrySelectsWithThePinnedMetadataSnapshot(t *testing.T) {\n1265:func TestCarryRefusesAnUnreadableMetadataBlob(t *testing.T) {\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"runtime/debug\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/version\"\n)\n\n// A modified build is not a comparable engine identity (spec\n// pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks, review round 2, N4).\nfunc TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds(t *testing.T) {\n\tinfo := func(settings ...debug.BuildSetting) *debug.BuildInfo { return &debug.BuildInfo{Settings: settings} }\n\tcases := []struct {\n\t\tname       string\n\t\tinfo       *debug.BuildInfo\n\t\twant       string\n\t\tverifiable bool\n\t}{\n\t\t{\"clean\", info(debug.BuildSetting{Key: \"vcs.revision\", Value: \"abc\"}, debug.BuildSetting{Key: \"vcs.modified\", Value: \"false\"}), version.Version + \"+abc\", true},\n\t\t{\"modified\", info(debug.BuildSetting{Key: \"vcs.revision\", Value: \"abc\"}, debug.BuildSetting{Key: \"vcs.modified\", Value: \"true\"}), version.Version + \"+abc.dirty\", false},\n\t\t{\"unstamped\", info(), version.Version, true},\n\t}\n\tfor _, tc := range cases {\n\t\tgot, verifiable := engineIdentityFrom(tc.info, true)\n\t\tif got != tc.want || verifiable != tc.verifiable {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: identity %q verifiable %v, want %q %v\", tc.name, got, verifiable, tc.want, tc.verifiable)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\npackage pose\n\nimport \"testing\"\n\n// A carried check is read as an observation of the head it ran at (spec\n// pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks R7); an executed one keeps the run's.\nfunc TestDeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead(t *testing.T) {\n\traw := []byte(`{\"schema_version\":1,\"generated_at\":\"2026-11-22T10:00:00Z\",\"git_head\":\"bbbb\",\"checks\":[` +\n\t\t`{\"id\":\"a/go/ok\",\"module\":\"a\",\"name\":\"ok\",\"severity\":\"required\",\"evidence_class\":\"unit\",\"outcome\":\"pass\"},` +\n\t\t`{\"id\":\"b/go/ok\",\"module\":\"b\",\"name\":\"ok\",\"severity\":\"required\",\"evidence_class\":\"unit\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"carried_from\":\"aaaa\",\"carried_generated_at\":\"2026-11-21T09:00:00Z\"}]}`)\n\tresults, err := ParseDeliveryValidationRun(raw, \".pose/results/delivery-validation.json\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif len(results) != 2 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"results = %+v\", results)\n\t}\n\tfor _, r := range results {\n\t\tswitch r.ID {\n\t\tcase \"a/go/ok\":\n\t\t\tif r.GitHead != \"bbbb\" || r.GeneratedAt != \"2026-11-22T10:00:00Z\" {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"executed check read as %s at %s\", r.GitHead, r.GeneratedAt)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\tcase \"b/go/ok\":\n\t\t\tif r.GitHead != \"aaaa\" || r.GeneratedAt != \"2026-11-21T09:00:00Z\" {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"carried check read as %s at %s, want the head it ran at\", r.GitHead, r.GeneratedAt)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\ndiff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 4621ed21..403846b6 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ pose new-knowledge <type> <slug>   # create handoff/note/decision-log\n pose check [--strict|--tolerant]   # structural integrity + matrix schema +\n                                    # task-map sync + spec graph + schema version\n pose validate [--strict|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module path] [--report] [--json-out f] [--junit f] [--sarif f]\n-              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev]] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n+              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev] | --carry] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n pose lint-spec <slug>|--all [--strict|--tolerant] [--required-only] [--ready-check] [--design-check]\n pose knowledge-check [--strict|--tolerant] [--max-overdue N]\n pose recurrence-check [--strict|--tolerant] [--window-days N] [--threshold T] [--flap-threshold N] [--include-pass]\n@@ -350,7 +350,9 @@ pose release-package-manifests --version X.Y.Z --checksums <checksums.txt> --out\n - `new-knowledge` — creates an artifact in [`.pose/knowledge/`](.pose/knowledge/) from [`.pose/templates/knowledge.md`](.pose/templates/knowledge.md) with mandatory frontmatter (`type`, `owner`, `sensitivity`, `created_at`, `last_reviewed_at`, `expires_at`). Computes `expires_at` from the TTL (default 30d, max 90d).\n - `validate` — runs the declarative matrix in [`validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json): per-stack checks, per-module overrides, severity (`required`/`optional`) and mode (`strict`/`tolerant`). `--json-out`/`--junit`/`--sarif <path>` (`--json <path>` still works as a deprecated alias of `--json-out <path>`) emit the versioned structured result (schema 1) from one canonical model: stable check IDs (`<module>/<stack>/<name>`), command metadata, timing, severity, distinguishable outcomes (`pass|fail|error|skipped` — infra failures never masquerade as check failures), deterministic skip reasons, bounded captured output and secret redaction (configured env values only; inherited environment never enters the result). Text output stays authoritative; machine formats are additive. POSE-specific semantics survive the JUnit/SARIF projections via documented extensions (classname suffix / `pose/*` properties).\n   **Runtime guardrails:** every check runs under a timeout (`timeoutSeconds` per check, `defaults.timeoutSeconds`, safe default 600s) and an output ceiling (`defaults.maxOutputBytes`, default 1 MiB); breaching either terminates the process group and records the explicit state (`limit_state: timeout|output-limit`). Checks marked `isolation: \"required\"` never run locally — they are skipped with a machine-readable reason and exported by `--emit-plan <file>`: an execution-plan envelope binding project, spec, check plan, matrix digest, git HEAD and an approval slot to be stamped with an expiring execution identity before the Harness may run it.\n-  **Changed scope:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` selects the minimum safe module set deterministically — modules containing changed files (tracked and untracked), transitive dependents via `dependsOn` edges in [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json), and policy widening (criticality `high` always runs). A change outside every module runs everything (uncertainty prefers safe execution); unselected checks are recorded as skipped with the selection reason and `--explain` prints every decision. Revisions are confined to a safe grammar; without the flags, full validation is unchanged.\n+  **Changed scope:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` selects the minimum safe module set deterministically — modules containing changed files (tracked and untracked), transitive dependents via `dependsOn` edges in [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json), and policy widening (criticality `high` always runs). Changed names are read NUL-delimited and a rename names both its source and its destination. Each changed file selects its most specific owning module, every module enclosing that owner (the root module encloses them all), every module beneath it (a gitlink or replaced directory changes what lies under it), and every module whose declared `dependsOn` contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, even after that dependency is deleted. A file no module owns selects the root module. Module metadata that does not decode stops the selection (a full run under `--carry`, an error under `--changed-from`). A change outside every module runs every module that does not declare `\"selfContained\": true` in its metadata (uncertainty prefers safe execution; the declaration states that the module's checks read only its own directory and its `dependsOn` modules); unselected checks are recorded as skipped with the selection reason and `--explain` prints every decision. Revisions are confined to a safe grammar; without the flags, full validation is unchanged.\n+\n+  **Carried checks:** `--carry --json-out <results_path>` refreshes the canonical result instead of rerunning the whole matrix. It uses the current canonical result as its base when the base is comparable: same schema, mode, matrix digest and `engine_version` (the engine version plus the VCS revision the binary was built from; a build of a modified tree never carries), unfiltered, not cancelled (a signal cancels the whole run, even an all-carried one), recorded `material_clean` (it validated an unchanged working copy of its own head: no tracked or untracked unignored material changed and HEAD did not move while it ran, as its reflog and every submodule's reflog show; mode changes count whatever `core.fileMode` says, and every submodule must hold its recorded commit with no nested submodule, checked both before the plan is read and when the run ends) with no unavailable material binding, with its `git_head` an ancestor of `HEAD`, a clean material working copy now, a case-sensitive filesystem with no case-folded directory on the path to a module or a dependency, no module reached through a symlink or sharing its directory with another module, no tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a module other than the root or in a declared `dependsOn` (or whose target leaves the repository), every submodule's tree included (a submodule that is not checked out or has nested submodules refuses), no declared dependency outside the repository or written as an unclean path or resolving through a symlink (tracked or ignored), only ASCII module and dependency paths, no index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, and no check id defined twice, and working module metadata equal to HEAD's. Changed names are read with every gitlink shown, whatever the Git configuration. The head is pinned before planning, and a run whose HEAD moved records its material bindings as unavailable. It runs the modules the changed-scope rules select between the base head and `HEAD`; the canonical result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings ignore (data files that are still regular files in the derived-record directories under `.pose/`: indexes, results, state, assessments and review records; the validation matrix stays material) are not changes. A module whose checks are not all in the base also runs. Every other check keeps the base result, its outcome included, and records `carried_from` (the head it ran at, kept through chained carries) and `carried_generated_at`; the delivery index reads that head for the result, so evidence freshness judges the commit a carried check really observed. A carried failure still fails the run. Any unmet condition runs everything, and `carry.reason` says why. `carry` records the base, the number of changed files and each selected module's reason, and `counts.carried` the reused checks. `--carry` does not combine with `--module`, `--stack`, `--workspace`, `--root-only`, `--changed-from` or `--changed-to`.\n \n   **Concurrency:** checks run up to `--jobs <n>` at a time (default: half the cores, bounded by available memory at about 1.5 GiB per check and by 8); results are reported and recorded in matrix order, whatever order they finish in, and the report records `jobs` and `wall_seconds`. `--jobs 1` and `--verbose` run one at a time. A check marked `exclusive: true` runs with nothing else running: earlier checks finish first, so its `when` can depend on them, which a concurrent check's cannot — a check's `when` is read as it starts. The run ends with its wall time beside the sum of its checks and the slowest checks. An interrupt or SIGTERM stops every running check's process group (on Windows, its process) and starts nothing more; those checks are recorded with `limit_state: cancelled`, the run is `fail` and exits 1, and a second signal acts at once. A default `--jobs` follows the cgroup's memory headroom and CPU quota where there is one.\n \ndiff --git a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nindex df424ce4..853f41f5 100644\n--- a/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n+++ b/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@ pose new-knowledge <type> <slug>   # cria handoff/note/decision-log em .pose/kno\n pose check [--strict|--tolerant]   # integridade estrutural + matrix schema +\n                                    # task-map sync + grafo de specs + schema version\n pose validate [--strict|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module path] [--report] [--json-out f] [--junit f] [--sarif f]\n-              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev]] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n+              [--changed-from rev [--changed-to rev] | --carry] [--jobs n] [--explain] [--emit-plan f]\n pose lint-spec <slug>|--all [--strict|--tolerant] [--required-only] [--ready-check] [--design-check]\n pose knowledge-check [--strict|--tolerant] [--max-overdue N]\n pose recurrence-check [--strict|--tolerant] [--window-days N] [--threshold T] [--flap-threshold N] [--include-pass]\n@@ -354,7 +354,9 @@ pose release-package-manifests --version X.Y.Z --checksums <checksums.txt> --out\n - `new-knowledge` — cria artefato em [`.pose/knowledge/`](.pose/knowledge/) a partir de [`.pose/templates/knowledge.md`](.pose/templates/knowledge.md) com frontmatter obrigatório (`type`, `owner`, `sensitivity`, `created_at`, `last_reviewed_at`, `expires_at`). Calcula `expires_at` pelo TTL (default 30d, máximo 90d).\n - `validate` — executa a matriz declarativa em [`validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json): checks por stack, overrides por módulo, severidade (`required`/`optional`) e modo (`strict`/`tolerant`). `--json-out`/`--junit`/`--sarif <path>` (`--json <path>` continua funcionando como alias depreciado de `--json-out <path>`) emitem o resultado estruturado versionado (schema 1) a partir de um único modelo canônico: IDs estáveis de check (`<module>/<stack>/<name>`), metadados de comando, tempo, severidade, outcomes distinguíveis (`pass|fail|error|skipped` — falha de infraestrutura nunca se disfarça de falha de check), motivos determinísticos de skip, saída capturada com limite e redação de segredos (apenas valores de env configurados; o ambiente herdado nunca entra no resultado). A saída em texto continua autoritativa; os formatos de máquina são aditivos. A semântica específica do POSE sobrevive às projeções JUnit/SARIF via extensões documentadas (sufixo de classname / propriedades `pose/*`).\n   **Guardrails de runtime:** todo check roda sob timeout (`timeoutSeconds` por check, `defaults.timeoutSeconds`, default seguro 600s) e teto de saída (`defaults.maxOutputBytes`, default 1 MiB); violar qualquer um encerra o process group e registra o estado explícito (`limit_state: timeout|output-limit`). Checks marcados `isolation: \"required\"` nunca rodam localmente — são pulados com motivo legível por máquina e exportados por `--emit-plan <file>`: um envelope de plano de execução vinculando projeto, spec, plano de checks, digest da matriz, git HEAD e um slot de aprovação a ser carimbado com identidade de execução expirável antes que o Harness possa executá-lo.\n-  **Escopo por mudança:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` seleciona deterministicamente o conjunto mínimo seguro de módulos — módulos com arquivos alterados (rastreados e não rastreados), dependentes transitivos via arestas `dependsOn` em [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json) e alargamento por política (criticidade `high` sempre roda). Uma mudança fora de todos os módulos roda tudo (na incerteza, prefere-se execução segura); checks não selecionados são registrados como skipped com o motivo da seleção e `--explain` imprime cada decisão. Revisões ficam confinadas a uma gramática segura; sem as flags, a validação completa é inalterada.\n+  **Escopo por mudança:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` seleciona deterministicamente o conjunto mínimo seguro de módulos — módulos com arquivos alterados (rastreados e não rastreados), dependentes transitivos via arestas `dependsOn` em [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json) e alargamento por política (criticidade `high` sempre roda). Os nomes alterados são lidos delimitados por NUL, e um rename nomeia a origem e o destino. Cada arquivo alterado seleciona o módulo dono mais específico, todo módulo que envolve esse dono (o módulo raiz envolve todos), todo módulo abaixo dele (um gitlink ou diretório substituído altera o que está abaixo) e todo módulo cujo `dependsOn` declarado o contém, está abaixo dele ou é a raiz `.`, mesmo depois que essa dependência é apagada. Um arquivo que nenhum módulo possui seleciona o módulo raiz. Metadados de módulo que não decodificam interrompem a seleção (execução completa com `--carry`, erro com `--changed-from`). Uma mudança fora de todos os módulos roda todo módulo que não declara `\"selfContained\": true` nos seus metadados (na incerteza, prefere-se execução segura; a declaração afirma que os checks do módulo só leem o próprio diretório e os módulos de `dependsOn`); checks não selecionados são registrados como skipped com o motivo da seleção e `--explain` imprime cada decisão. Revisões ficam confinadas a uma gramática segura; sem as flags, a validação completa é inalterada.\n+\n+  **Checks carregados:** `--carry --json-out <results_path>` renova o resultado canônico em vez de rodar a matriz inteira de novo. Ele usa o resultado canônico atual como base quando a base é comparável: mesmo schema, modo, digest da matriz e `engine_version` (a versão do motor mais a revisão VCS da qual o binário foi compilado; um build de árvore modificada nunca carrega), sem filtro, não cancelada (um sinal cancela o run inteiro, mesmo um só com checks carregados), com `material_clean` registrado (validou uma cópia de trabalho inalterada do próprio head: nenhum material rastreado ou não rastreado e não ignorado mudou, e o HEAD não se moveu durante o run, segundo o reflog dele e de todo submódulo; mudanças de modo contam qualquer que seja `core.fileMode`, e todo submódulo precisa estar no commit registrado, sem submódulo aninhado, verificado antes da leitura do plano e no fim do run) e sem binding de material indisponível, com `git_head` ancestral de `HEAD` cópia de trabalho limpa agora nos paths materiais sistema de arquivos que diferencia maiúsculas, sem diretório com casefold no caminho até um módulo ou uma dependência, nenhum módulo alcançado por symlink ou compartilhando diretório com outro módulo, nenhum symlink rastreado cujo path ou alvo esteja num módulo que não seja a raiz ou num `dependsOn` declarado (ou cujo alvo saia do repositório), inclusive na árvore de todo submódulo (um submódulo sem checkout ou com submódulos aninhados recusa), nenhuma dependência declarada fora do repositório ou escrita como path não limpo ou que resolve por symlink (rastreado ou ignorado), apenas paths ASCII de módulo e dependência, nenhuma entrada de índice marcada assume-unchanged ou skip-worktree, e nenhum id de check definido duas vezes e metadados de módulo da cópia de trabalho iguais aos do HEAD. Os nomes alterados são lidos com todo gitlink visível, qualquer que seja a configuração do Git. O head é fixado antes do planejamento, e um run cujo HEAD se moveu registra seus bindings de material como indisponíveis. Roda os módulos que as regras de escopo por mudança selecionam entre o head da base e `HEAD`; o arquivo do resultado canônico e os registros administrativos derivados que o binding de material ignora (arquivos de dados ainda regulares nos diretórios de registros derivados sob `.pose/`: índices, resultados, estado, assessments e registros de revisão; a matriz de validação continua material) não contam como mudança. Um módulo cujos checks não estão todos na base também roda. Todo outro check mantém o resultado da base, inclusive o desfecho, e registra `carried_from` (o head em que rodou, mantido em carregamentos encadeados) e `carried_generated_at`; o índice de entrega lê esse head no resultado, então o frescor da evidência julga o commit que um check carregado realmente observou. Uma falha carregada continua reprovando o run. Qualquer condição não atendida roda tudo, e `carry.reason` diz por quê. `carry` registra a base, o número de arquivos alterados e o motivo de cada módulo selecionado, e `counts.carried` os checks reaproveitados. `--carry` não combina com `--module`, `--stack`, `--workspace`, `--root-only`, `--changed-from` ou `--changed-to`.\n \n   **Concorrência:** os checks rodam até `--jobs <n>` ao mesmo tempo (padrão: metade dos núcleos, limitada pela memória disponível, cerca de 1,5 GiB por check, e por 8); os resultados são mostrados e registrados na ordem da matriz, seja qual for a ordem em que terminem, e o relatório registra `jobs` e `wall_seconds`. `--jobs 1` e `--verbose` rodam um de cada vez. Um check marcado `exclusive: true` roda sem nenhum outro em execução: os checks anteriores terminam antes, então seu `when` pode depender deles, o que o de um check concorrente não pode — o `when` de um check é lido quando ele vai começar. A execução termina com seu tempo de parede ao lado da soma dos checks e os checks mais lentos. Uma interrupção ou SIGTERM encerra o grupo de processos de cada check em execução (no Windows, seu processo) e não inicia mais nada; esses checks são registrados com `limit_state: cancelled`, a execução fica `fail` e sai com 1, e um segundo sinal age na hora. O `--jobs` padrão segue a folga de memória e a cota de CPU do cgroup, quando há um.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\nindex f252f70a..c6381d05 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n@@ -129,6 +129,7 @@ var commandHelpCatalog = map[string]CommandHelp{\n \t\t\t{\"--json-out <path>\", \"Write structured validation outcome to the specified JSON path\", \"Grava o resultado da validação no caminho JSON especificado\"},\n \t\t\t{\"--json <path>\", \"Deprecated alias of --json-out <path>\", \"Alias depreciado de --json-out <path>\"},\n \t\t\t{\"--changed-from <rev>\", \"Validate only modules affected between git revisions\", \"Valida apenas módulos afetados entre as revisões git\"},\n+\t\t\t{\"--carry\", \"Refresh the canonical result: run what changed since it and carry the other checks with the head they ran at\", \"Renova o resultado canônico: roda o que mudou desde ele e carrega os demais checks com o head em que rodaram\"},\n \t\t\t{\"--jobs <n>\", \"Run up to n checks at once (default: from cores and available memory)\", \"Roda até n checks ao mesmo tempo (padrão: conforme núcleos e memória disponível)\"},\n \t\t\t{\"--verbose\", \"Stream each check's output as it runs; by default it is captured and a failing check's tail is shown\", \"Transmite a saída de cada check durante a execução; por padrão ela é capturada e o final da saída de um check que falha é exibido\"},\n \t\t},\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:45:separate mechanism carrying separate self-referential data (JSON policy\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:32:when the spec closes, and retired when the ADR and `docs-site/docs/cli.md` carry\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:113:Three persistence paths exist, and they carry different things — worth keeping\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:419:- `pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_integrity.go` — findings already carry\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
