{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | head -45; git show dec2e64:POSE.md | sha256sum; git show dec2e64:pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | sha256sum; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | tail -25; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | sed -n '704,797p'; rg -n 'Material|CarriedFrom' pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation*.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review*evidence*.go | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-23 11:36:06.325276966 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-23 11:36:06.367056308 -0300\n@@ -574,19 +574,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\nbd511396b09b73b64ee4e8e8ce235c015b7a3b608683fe20172b8c7dd5a0f8f3  -\naab2fca8d1f09a6386fa0cc10f17819c367fcd52a0db5e40b16308ec1990f8d6  -\n   232\t- R9 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun\n   233\t- R10 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun\n   234\t\n   235\tR9 is enforced by `safeGitRevRE` in `planCarry` before any Git call; the not-an-ancestor case drives a forged head through it. R10 is the `base without engine version` case.\n   236\t\n   237\t### Known gaps\n   238\tReview bundles and closeout consume the per-check head through the delivery index. No separate end-to-end test seals a bundle over a carried record.\n   239\t\n   240\t## 7. Final Report\n   241\t\n   242\t### Delivered scope\n   243\t`pose validate --carry` refreshes the canonical structured result. It runs the modules the changed-scope rules select since the canonical base and carries the other checks with their outcome and the head where they ran. The changed set ignores the result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings already ignore. Any doubt about the base runs everything, and the record says why. Modules can declare `selfContained` to stop being widened by changes outside every module. The delivery index reads a carried result as an observation of its own head. The record now names the engine version together with its build revision.\n   244\t\n   245\t### Files and modules changed\n   246\t`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n   247\t\n   248\t### Validation executed\n   249\tSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n   250\t\n   251\t### Residual risks\n   252\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   253\t\n   254\t### Follow-ups\n   255\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   256\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   704\t\treturn true\n   705\t}\n   706\t\n   707\t// workingFileDiffersFromHead reports whether rel in the working copy differs\n   708\t// from its blob at head; absent on both sides is equal.\n   709\tfunc workingFileDiffersFromHead(root, head, rel string) (bool, error) {\n   710\t\tpresent, err := inTree(root, head, rel)\n   711\t\tif err != nil {\n   712\t\t\treturn true, err\n   713\t\t}\n   714\t\tworking, werr := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(rel)))\n   715\t\tif !present {\n   716\t\t\t// Absent from the commit: equal only when absent from the copy too.\n   717\t\t\treturn !errors.Is(werr, os.ErrNotExist), nil\n   718\t\t}\n   719\t\tcommitted, cerr := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"show\", head+\":\"+rel).Output()\n   720\t\tif cerr != nil {\n   721\t\t\treturn true, fmt.Errorf(\"%s at %s is unreadable: %v\", rel, head, cerr)\n   722\t\t}\n   723\t\tif werr != nil {\n   724\t\t\treturn true, nil\n   725\t\t}\n   726\t\treturn !bytes.Equal(working, committed), nil\n   727\t}\n   728\t\n   729\t// movementWitness summarizes the reflog lengths of HEAD and of every\n   730\t// checked-out submodule's HEAD; \"\" when any cannot be read, so the witness\n   731\t// never passes by default.\n   732\tfunc movementWitness(root, head string) string {\n   733\t\tparent := headReflogLength(root)\n   734\t\tif parent < 0 || head == \"\" {\n   735\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   736\t\t}\n   737\t\tparts := []string{fmt.Sprintf(\".=%d\", parent)}\n   738\t\tlinks, err := gitlinks(root, head)\n   739\t\tif err != nil {\n   740\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   741\t\t}\n   742\t\tsubs := make([]string, 0, len(links))\n   743\t\tfor sub := range links {\n   744\t\t\tsubs = append(subs, sub)\n   745\t\t}\n   746\t\tsort.Strings(subs)\n   747\t\tfor _, sub := range subs {\n   748\t\t\trepo := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(sub))\n   749\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(repo, \".git\")); err != nil {\n   750\t\t\t\tparts = append(parts, sub+\"=absent\")\n   751\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   752\t\t\t}\n   753\t\t\tn := headReflogLength(repo)\n   754\t\t\tif n < 0 {\n   755\t\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   756\t\t\t}\n   757\t\t\tparts = append(parts, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s=%d\", sub, n))\n   758\t\t}\n   759\t\treturn strings.Join(parts, \",\")\n   760\t}\n   761\t\n   762\t// scopeMetadataAt reads the module metadata of commit head: absent is empty,\n   763\t// undecodable is an error.\n   764\tfunc scopeMetadataAt(root, head string) (scopeMetadata, error) {\n   765\t\tvar meta scopeMetadata\n   766\t\tconst rel = \".pose/indexes/module-metadata.json\"\n   767\t\t// Absence is read from the pinned tree; a listed blob that cannot be read\n   768\t\t// is an error, never an empty policy (review round 18, N52).\n   769\t\tpresent, err := inTree(root, head, rel)\n   770\t\tif err != nil {\n   771\t\t\treturn meta, err\n   772\t\t}\n   773\t\tif !present {\n   774\t\t\treturn meta, nil\n   775\t\t}\n   776\t\traw, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"show\", head+\":\"+rel).Output()\n   777\t\tif err != nil {\n   778\t\t\treturn meta, fmt.Errorf(\"module metadata at %s is unreadable: %v\", head, err)\n   779\t\t}\n   780\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &meta); err != nil {\n   781\t\t\treturn scopeMetadata{}, fmt.Errorf(\"module metadata does not decode: %v\", err)\n   782\t\t}\n   783\t\treturn meta, nil\n   784\t}\n   785\t\n   786\t// inTree reports whether rel is an entry of head's tree, reading the tree,\n   787\t// not the blob; a tree that cannot be read is an error.\n   788\tfunc inTree(root, head, rel string) (bool, error) {\n   789\t\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"ls-tree\", \"-z\", head, \"--\", rel).Output()\n   790\t\tif err != nil {\n   791\t\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"the tree of %s is unreadable: %v\", head, err)\n   792\t\t}\n   793\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(strings.TrimRight(string(out), \"\\x00\")) != \"\", nil\n   794\t}\nrg: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review*evidence*.go: No such file or directory (os error 2)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:23:\t\tMaterialProvenance map[string]string `json:\"material_provenance,omitempty\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:33:\t\t\tCarriedFrom        string `json:\"carried_from,omitempty\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:46:\t\tif check.CarriedFrom != \"\" {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:47:\t\t\thead, generated = check.CarriedFrom, check.CarriedGeneratedAt\npose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go:49:\t\tresults = append(results, DeliveryValidationResult{ID: check.ID, Module: check.Module, Check: check.Name, EvidenceClass: check.EvidenceClass, Severity: check.Severity, Outcome: check.Outcome, GitHead: head, GeneratedAt: generated, ProvenanceDigest: run.ProvenanceDigest, ScopeProvenance: run.ScopeProvenance, MaterialProvenance: run.MaterialProvenance, Report: relative})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
