}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\"}, {\"action\": \"modified\", \"path\": \"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"}], \"diff_digest\": \"sha256:2c9daac4b347000bd85d9391a48ae39292eb798f9ca5962375dae76297b8ab36\", \"material_digest\": \"sha256:bab398df7e176f271bd5b22cd1bee529a893f2c4bcbf600fea570ad0f5e650e7\", \"material_inputs\": {\"names\": [\".pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\", \".pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json\", \".pose/indexes/generation.json\", \".pose/indexes/spec-graph.json\", \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\", \".pose/results/delivery-validation.json\", \".pose/results/pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks-matrix.md\", \".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\", \"POSE.md\", \"locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_engine_identity_test.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run_test.go\", \"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\", \"pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"]}}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo remaining blocker established. The unreadable-metadata defect is fixed. Two existing low-severity follow-ups remain accepted through **2026-12-15**:\n\n- **N55:** `--carry --report` presents carried checks as executed commands without their original head and time.\n- **N56:** Dedicated end-to-end coverage for sealing, verifying and closing over a carried record remains missing.\n\nIndependent focused tests, `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...` and artifact-check passed. Full-matrix validation relies on the sealed evidence under the brief’s sandbox allowance. The checkout remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\nApplied the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. Consulted knowledge governance and existing follow-ups.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N55\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1623,\n      \"summary\": \"validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in Commands and renders their prior outcomes and durations without carried_from or carried_generated_at. A newly dated --carry --report therefore presents reused observations as commands executed by this run. This remains spec follow-up F2.\",\n      \"action\": \"Implement F2: exclude carried checks from the executed-command summary and label reused results with their original head and time.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N56\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\",\n      \"line\": 255,\n      \"summary\": \"The delivery reader directly tests carried head and time, but no dedicated end-to-end fixture seals a bundle, verifies it and checks closeout over a carried record. This remains spec follow-up F1.\",\n      \"action\": \"Implement F1: add the carried-record seal, verify and closeout-check fixture, including rejection of misattributed evidence.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin. The owned remediation remains F2 at spec line 256; retained as N55.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Source inspection of validationSummaryOf at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1619-1636 confirms the report-provenance defect remains; retained as N55 under F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623 appends every non-skipped command without testing CarriedFrom, and lines 1626-1636 omit original head and time; retained as N55.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N51\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validationSummaryOf at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1619-1636 remains unchanged in the relevant behavior. F2 at spec line 256 owns the remediation; retained as N55.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N52\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"scopeMetadataAt at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:769-778 determines presence from the pinned tree and returns an error when a listed blob cannot be read. workingFileDiffersFromHead at lines 710-721 does likewise. Independently ran go test ./internal/cli -run 'CarryRefusesAnUnreadableMetadataBlob|CarrySelectsWithThePinnedMetadataSnapshot|DeliveryValidation' -count=1 in pose-mcp; passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N53\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still loses carried provenance in the report projection. This is the existing F2 risk retained as N55.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N54\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The spec explicitly retains the missing end-to-end fixture at lines 237-238 and 255. delivery_validation_run_test.go directly covers parsing head and time, rather than seal/verify/closeout. Retained as N56.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, requirements R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, CLI help, English and pt-BR manuals and embedded copies. Swept flag confinement, base eligibility, unreadable metadata, pinned metadata selection, dirty material and unavailable bindings, cancellation, HEAD and submodule movement, gitlinks, nested submodules, symlinks, case and Unicode aliases, hidden index entries, clean and escaping dependency paths, renames and quoted names, manifest-free moduleOverrides, nested and root ownership, stack/check identity changes, criticality and transitive dependency widening, administrative exclusions, chained carries, failures and counts, delivery consumption, scheduler behavior and canonical publication. Concurrent readers receive a complete atomic record; publication retains its governance guard and policy recheck. Independently ran focused carry/scope/validate/material tests, engine identity and concurrency/publication tests, delivery-reader/material tests, the latest metadata regressions with -count=1, go vet ./..., go build ./..., artifact-check, assess-design, suggest-review and recurrence-check. Recurrence-check flagged zero keys. Reviewed changed debt markers directly. Scratch creation and go run failed with Read-only file system, preventing assessment-copy and full-matrix reruns; used the explicitly permitted sealed canonical validation evidence. No new blocker was established. Report provenance and dedicated carried-record closeout coverage remain the two owned low risks. Final git status was clean.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined D1-D3 and their eligibility and selection premises. Verified pinned metadata, conservative alias refusals and material-clean checks in source and focused tests. Actual check inputs respecting declared module/dependency boundaries remain an explicit instance assumption; arbitrary external inputs and environmental nondeterminism are outside this cache contract. N55 and N56 are accepted low risks. Full-matrix verification relies on sealed evidence, not an independent rerun.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected carried entries, scheduler exclusion, cancellation finalization and canonical publication. Carried entries are silent and bypass execution; publication retains the governance write guard, policy recheck and authoritative atomic writer. Focused cancellation, concurrency and publication tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Result fields and CLI functionality are additive. Legacy records remain readable and cannot become carry bases without the required identity and cleanliness fields. The delivery reader uses original carried head and time; its direct regression passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed incompatible flags, revision confinement, absent and unreadable metadata, unusable bases and conservative fallback reasons. The latest unreadable-blob and pinned-metadata regressions passed independently with -count=1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced canonical JSON through ParseDeliveryValidationRun into delivery results and material provenance. Direct carried-head/time tests passed. Dedicated carried-record sealing and closeout coverage remains accepted follow-up N56.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N55\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined flag parsing, result schema additions, old-record parsing and engine identity comparison. Existing CLI, file and MCP consumers retain compatible contracts. Invalid selection metadata now errors or forces a full run as explicitly required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused carry, changed-scope, material, engine identity, cancellation, concurrency, publication and delivery-reader tests passed. go vet ./... and go build ./... passed. Reviewed negative selection and provenance paths; no remaining correctness blocker was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses repeated whole-matrix execution by preserving original observations while selecting changed inputs. D2 rejects matrix and engine drift; D3 makes root-change exemptions explicit. The cheapest unsupported shortcut would reuse an observation for changed or unverified material; eligibility and selection regressions cover those shortcuts. There is no dedicated carried-record seal/verify/closeout adversarial journey yet; that boundary is retained as N56.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records the structural evidence decision: carried checks retain their original head while the current run computes material bindings, justified by sound changed-scope selection and explicit declarations.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared requirements, ADR, help and both language manuals with runtime selection, eligibility and provenance behavior. Changed carry documentation is mirrored in embedded copies. The root English manual's contributor-mode section differs from the scaffold by an existing instance-specific section outside this change. F1 and F2 are explicitly owned and dated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N55\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Mapped R1-R10 to implementation and relevant regressions, including refusal flags, fallback eligibility, selection, preserved outcomes and origins, counts, declarations, delivery reading, all-carried behavior and compatibility. Focused tests passed; N56 preserves the disclosed end-to-end coverage gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source changes stay within validation planning/results, shared changed-scope selection, delivery consumption, tests and corresponding documentation. The ADR is justified by the evidence contract. Derived records in the broader Git range were distinguished from the sealed implementation scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined revision confinement, path containment, dependency escapes, symlink and case aliases, hidden index entries, unreadable Git objects and publication authority. Uncertainty conservatively refuses reuse. No new dependency or sensitive-data exposure was identified in the reviewed diff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module-level reuse extends the existing selector and uses whole-matrix and engine comparison instead of introducing an arbitrary-input cache. Per-check input hashing would require a larger declaration contract; manual merging would lose provenance. Conservative alias refusals trade optimization coverage for simpler safety reasoning. Revisit this choice if actual inputs cannot be represented by the declared boundaries or finer reuse becomes a requirement.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required command exited 0. It reported 985 warnings and resolved the trailer range through a later derived-record commit, as disclosed in the brief. This is not evidence that the sealed implementation scope expanded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess design --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json successfully. Its digest matches the sealed structural evidence and it reports SD-253b523c.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation failed with Read-only file system. Discovery was not run in the sealed checkout because it can persist assessment outputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required assessment copy could not be created. Avoided modifying the sealed checkout; integration judgment uses source tracing, focused delivery tests and sealed integration evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment copy could not be created. Reviewed changed implementation markers and the spec's owned follow-ups directly; did not persist assessment or state files.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate must run after POSE records and verifies this conclusion. The reviewer did not record an attestation or apply closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records this review's attestation, as required by the brief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully and applied the selected review workflow, backend-go, security and documentation-style rules, with delivery-evidence guidance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the sealed canonical strict-validation result under the brief's explicit sandbox allowance. An independent full-matrix rerun was not completed: scratch creation and go run failed with Read-only file system. Independently ran focused tests, go vet ./... and go build ./... successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the sealed canonical component-validation result under the brief's sandbox allowance. Independently passed go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material'; focused engine identity, cancellation, concurrency and canonical-publication tests; go test ./internal/pose -run 'DeliveryValidationRun|Material'; the latest metadata regressions with -count=1; go vet ./...; and go build ./.... This does not claim an independent full component-matrix rerun.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
